I.      Course Title:
        Basic Static Timing Analysis 3.0

II.     Course Developer:
        Krishna Atreya

III.    Minimum Hardware Requirements:
	Installation requirement - 1Mbytes. 
	Lab requirement - retain at least 250Mbytes for the course 
	duration for saving of intermediate files, designs, and for the software.

IV.     Software Products Required:
	An X-Window environment is required to run the software.
	This course uses one of the following licenses:
		Tempus_Timing_Signoff_L
		Tempus_Timing_Signoff_XL
		Tempus_Timing_Signoff_TSO

        Reference Manuals that should be available (or online):
		Tempus User Guide

V.      Loading and Set Up of Database
        Follow the instructions in the first lab.
 
VI.     Checking the software installation:
	Modify the class_setup file to point to the following:
	Cadence Tempus or SSV installation
	Then, run:
	source class_setup
	checkSysConf 

	checkSysConf will tell you if your tools have met the necessary requirements.
	The labs in the class might still work if certain installation requirements are not met.
	But, please make sure when running production designs, to make sure they are met.

	After the Cadence software and licenses are setup properly, continue to run the labs.
  	 
